    ],
    "speak": "What happened to the gases that eat the ozone layer, once the world agreed to ban them?"
   },
   {
    "ask": {
     "intro": "In 1989 the world used more than one and a half million tonnes a year.",
     "question": "Draw the line on to 2021.",
     "on": "line_1",
     "from": 1989,
     "store": "g",
     "after": "keep",
     "default": "1500,1350,1200,1050,900,800,700,600,500,450,400",
     "right": "Close: you were only {g.off} thousand tonnes off on average. It really did crash almost to the floor.",
     "wrong": "You were {g.off} thousand tonnes off on average. The line drops almost to the floor."
    }
   },
   {
    "animate": {
     "stage": 1
    },
    "duration": 2
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "endpt",
     "drop"
    ],
    "speak": "By 2021 it was about seventeen thousand tonnes: a fall of ninety-nine percent."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "montreal"
    ],
    "speak": "Why 1989? That year the Montreal Protocol came into force, to phase out CFCs from fridges and spray cans."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "every"
    ],
    "speak": "In time every country in the United Nations signed it, the first treaty ever to manage that."
   },
   {
    "erase": [
     "axes",
     "line_1",
     "endpt",
     "drop",
     "montreal",
     "every"
    ]
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "tl",
     "mt1",
     "holeic",
     "ml1"
    ],
    "speak": "They moved fast because, in 1985, scientists had found a hole in the ozone over Antarctica, letting through the ultraviolet light that causes skin cancer."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "mt2",
     "ml2"
    ],
    "speak": "And it worked: around 2000, the hole stopped growing."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "mt3",
     "now",
     "ml3"
    ],
    "speak": "But the old gases linger in the sky for decades. The hole over Antarctica should heal only around 2066."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "brace",
     "yrs40"
    ],
    "speak": "So a few years of action stopped the damage, but the sky needs another forty years to heal."
   }
